{
  "total": 67,
  "totalPage": 2,
  "page": 2,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09588",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3719,
      "bookHadithIndex": 51,
      "text": "Ibn Abbas said:The apostle of allah (ﷺ) forbade drinking from the mouth of a water-skin, and riding the animal which feeds on filth and eating the animal which is killed in confinement. Abu Dawud said: Jallalah means an animal which eats filth and impurities",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3719-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3719-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3719-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3719-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09589",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3720,
      "bookHadithIndex": 52,
      "text": "Abu Sa’id al-Khudri said :The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited drinking by inverting the heads of skin vessels",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3720-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3720-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3720-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3720-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (5625) Sahih Muslim (2023)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0958a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3721,
      "bookHadithIndex": 53,
      "text": "A man of the Ansar quoting from his father said that the Prophet (ﷺ) called for a skin-vessel on the day of the battle of Uhud. He then said:Invert the head of the vessel and he drank from its mouth",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3721-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3721-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Munkar"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3721-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3721-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0958b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3722,
      "bookHadithIndex": 54,
      "text": "Abu sa’id al-Khudri said:The apostle of Allah (ﷺ) forbade drinking from the broken place (of a cup) and blowing into a drink",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3722-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3722-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3722-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3722-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0958c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3723,
      "bookHadithIndex": 55,
      "text": "Ibn Abi Laila said:Whan Hudhaifah was in al-Mada’in, he asked for water. A peasant brought him a silver vessel. He threw it away and said: I threw it away, for I prohibited (him) but he did not stop. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade to wear silk or brocade, and to drink from gold and silver vessels. He said: Others have them in this world and you will have them in the next",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3723-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3723-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3723-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (5632) Sahih Muslim (2067)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0958d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3724,
      "bookHadithIndex": 56,
      "text": "Jabir b. ‘abd Allah said:The Prophet (ﷺ) went to visit a man of the Ansar accompanied by one of his Companions who was watering his garden. The Messenger of Allah(ﷺ) said: If you have any water which has remained over night in a skin (we should like it), or shall sip (from a streamlet)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3724-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3724-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3724-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (5621)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0958e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3725,
      "bookHadithIndex": 57,
      "text": "Narrated Abdullah ibn AbuAwfa: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: The supplier of the people is the last (man) to drink",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3725-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3725-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3725-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f0958f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3726,
      "bookHadithIndex": 58,
      "text": "Anas b. Malik said:The Prophet (ﷺ) was brought milk that was mixed with water. A nomad Arab was on his right and Abu Bakr was on his left. He himself drank and gave it to the nomad Arab, and said: He who is on the right , then he who is on his right then he who is on his right",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3726-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3726-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3726-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3726-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (5619) Sahih Muslim (2029)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09590",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3727,
      "bookHadithIndex": 59,
      "text": "Anas b.Malik said :when the prophet (ﷺ) drank, he used to breathe three times in the course of a drink and say : It is more whole some ,thrist-quenching and healthier",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3727-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3727-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3727-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (5631) Sahih Muslim (2028)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09591",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3728,
      "bookHadithIndex": 60,
      "text": "Narrated Abdullah ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade blowing or breathing into a vessel",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3728-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3728-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3728-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3728-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09592",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3729,
      "bookHadithIndex": 61,
      "text": "’Abd Allah b. Busr from Banu Sulaim said:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to my father and he was a guest with him. He offered food to him and brought hais. He then brought a drink which he drank and he gave it to the one on his right. He ate dried dates and began to put the kernels on the back of his ring finger and middle finger. When he got up, my father also got up, and held the rein of his mount. He said : Pray to Allah for me. He said : O Allah, bless them in what you provided them, and have mercy on them",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3729-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3729-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3729-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3729-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim (2042)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09593",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3730,
      "bookHadithIndex": 62,
      "text": "Narrated Abdullah ibn Abbas: I was in the house of Maymunah. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) accompanied by Khalid ibn al-Walid entered. Two roasted long-tailed lizards (dabb) placed on the sticks were brought to him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) spat. Khalid said: I think that you abominate it, Messenger of Allah. He said: Yes. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought milk, and he drank (it). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) then said: When one of you eats food, he should say: O Allah, bless us in it, and give us food (or nourishment) better than it. When he is given milk to drink he should say: O Allah! bless us in it and give us more of it, for no food or drink satisfies like milk. Abu Dawud said: This is the Musaddad's version",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3730-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3730-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3730-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09594",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3731,
      "bookHadithIndex": 63,
      "text": "Jabir reported the Prophet (ﷺ) as saying:Shut your door and make mention of Allah's name, for the devil does not open a door which has been shut; extinguish your lamp and make mention of Allah's name, cover up your vessel even by a piece of wood that you just put on it and make mention of Allah's name, and tie up your water-skin mentioning Allah's name",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3731-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3731-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3731-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3731-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (5623) Sahih Muslim (2012)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09595",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3732,
      "bookHadithIndex": 64,
      "text": "Jabir b.’Abd Allah reported the Prophet (ﷺ)as saying this version is not complete ‘’for the devil does not open a shut door, or loosen a water-skin, or uncover a vessel, for a mouse sets a house on fire over its inhabitants’’",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3732-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3732-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3732-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3732-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim (2012)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09596",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3733,
      "bookHadithIndex": 65,
      "text": "Jabir b.Abd Allah reported the Prophet (ﷺ) as saying:Gather your children when darkness spreads, or in the evening (according to Musaddad), for the jinn are abroad and seize them",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3733-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3733-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3733-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (3316) Sahih Muslim (2012)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09597",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3734,
      "bookHadithIndex": 66,
      "text": "Jabir said:We were with Prophet (ﷺ) and he asked for something to drink. A man from the company asked: Should we not give you nabidh (drink made from dates) to drink ? He replied : Yes . The man went quickly and bought a cup of nabidh. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Why did you not cover it up even by putting a piece of wood on it ? Abu Dawud said: Al-Asma'i's version has: \"You put it on it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3734-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3734-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3734-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3734-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (5605) Sahih Muslim (2011)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c55add1a4c9c86f09598",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 3735,
      "bookHadithIndex": 67,
      "text": "Narrated Aisha, Ummul Mu'minin: The water from as-Suqya' was considered sweetest by the Prophet (ﷺ). Qutaybah said: it was a well on two days' journey from Medina",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3735-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-27-3735-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}